--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [class.mi]/3 (Example 2: `class D : public A, public L'): a class
can be a direct and an indirect base; D has two L subobjects.  The
mem-initializer `L(3)' names the direct one ([class.base.init]/2), `A::next'
the member of A's one ([class.mi]/5), and the implicit copy constructor and
copy assignment operator copy both ([class.copy.ctor]/14,
[class.copy.assign]/12).  The front end rejected the class.  g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept this program (warning: direct base 'L' inaccessible due to
ambiguity), and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
